An indicator that shows a loading state.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/loader)

<%= embed AppicaUI::LoaderPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Loader()
Loader(variant: :dots, current_color: true, class: "text-3xl")
```

Loader is an indeterminate progress indicator - it conveys "working on it" without a percentage. It comes in
two shapes via `variant:` - `:bar` (a track with a sweeping fill, the default) and `:dots` (three dots flowing
left to right). Both read a little more like progress than a [Spinner](<%= page_path(:spinner) %>), so they
suit section- and status-level waits.

It's sized by font-size - set a `text-*` class (or inherit `1em`) - and `current_color: true` makes it match
the surrounding text instead of the primary accent. The shapes are SVG with SMIL `<animate>` elements, so they
loop with no JavaScript; under `prefers-reduced-motion` a static frame is shown instead.

