## API reference

Loader renders a single `<span role="status">`; other attributes are forwarded to it.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `variant:` | `:bar`, `:dots` | `:bar` | The animated shape. |
| `current_color:` | `Boolean` | `false` | Inherit the surrounding text color instead of the primary accent. |
| `aria_label:` | `String` | `"Loading"` | Accessible name for the status region. |
| `class:` | `String` | - | Extra classes, merged via tailwind_merge. Set a `text-*` size here. |

## Accessibility

- The loader is a `role="status"` live region labelled "Loading"; pass a more specific `aria_label:`
  ("Uploading files") when it helps.
- When a loader replaces a section's content, keep one labelled status in the region rather than several.
- A loader beside text that already states the status can be `aria_hidden: true` to avoid a duplicate announcement.
- The animation is replaced by a static frame when the user prefers reduced motion.
